From: Fanasina <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475-xiaomi-diting: Drop the MTE carveout

sm8450.dtsi reserves 512 MiB at 0xc0000000 (mte_mem, no-map) for the MTE tag
storage of the reference platform. Nothing in Linux uses it on diting: the
node has no phandle and no memory-region user. Removed with fdtput on the
installed DTB (MemTotal was 6557532 kB before), the phone booted with the
512 MiB back and survived stress-ng --vm 4 --vm-bytes 90% for two minutes, so
the firmware does not protect the region on this unit. Drop it.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts
@@ -44,6 +44,14 @@
 /delete-node/ &xbl_ramdump_mem;
 /delete-node/ &xbl_sc_mem;
 
+/*
+ * MTE tag storage carveout of the SM8450 reference (512 MiB at 0xc0000000).
+ * Nothing in Linux uses it here (no phandle, no memory-region user) and the
+ * firmware does not protect it on this unit: removing it from the DTB gave
+ * back 512 MiB of RAM and survived a stress-ng run over 90 % of the memory.
+ */
+/delete-node/ &mte_mem;
+
 / {
 	model = "Xiaomi 12T Pro / Redmi K50 Ultra";
 	compatible = "xiaomi,diting", "qcom,sm8475";
